# Seven-lens audit protocol

When the user asks to run, fix, verify, close, or continue a seven-lens cycle:

1. Read `docs/seven-lens-review-playbook.md`,
   `docs/cursor-seven-lens-audit-workflow.md`, and
   `docs/cursor-seven-lens-prompts.md` before acting.
2. If the cycle was BLOCKED, read the active Codex verification report in
   `docs/seven-lens-reports/` and the cycle record in `docs/seven-lens-records/`.
3. Run `python tools/seven_lens_protocol.py plan --cycle <N> --output
   docs/seven-lens-records/cycle-<NN>-*.json` before reading source.
4. Work in exactly one role per chat: AUDITOR, FIXER, VERIFIER, or CLOSER.
   Stop at the role boundary. Never describe your own fix pass as independent.
5. The AUDITOR is read-only for application source and tests. Complete every
   generated part and every L1-L7 record before proposing fixes. Every L2/L4/L7
   conclusion must quote `entry_event -> consumer_path`; without a concrete
   consumer path the result is `INCOMPLETE`, not `NO_FINDING`.
6. The FIXER implements only recorded findings and adds isolated behavioral
   evidence. Every probe must fail on the pre-fix commit, assert the final
   algorithm consumer (not a label, flag, or dataset stamp alone), and restore
   full state in `finally`.
7. The VERIFIER uses a fresh chat/context, reads final source rather than relying
   on the fix summary, reproduces failures through the real UI entry path, runs
   edit-after-switch traces, and inspects raw browser trace artifact JSON.
8. The CLOSER runs both:
   `python tools/seven_lens_protocol.py check --phase close --record <record>`
   and `python tools/seven_lens_protocol.py check-all --require-artifacts`.
   May close only when both exit 0. Then updates `docs/seven-lens-test-results.md`,
   pushes the cycle branch, and merges the PR to `dev` after CI passes.
   Every evidence command must be executed through
   `tools/seven_lens_evidence.py`; never synthesize evidence rows or success
   fields with a record-building script.
9. Never set `SEVEN_LENS_REVIEWED` in the manual ledger unless
   `check-all --require-artifacts` passes for that cycle's record.
10. Green automated tests are evidence, not a seven-lens review. Never infer "no
    bugs" or reviewed status from test results alone. Never accept a partial
    engine regression (e.g. 166/168) when the suite mutates shared DOM state.
11. Work against `dev`. Never target or modify `main` for this audit program.
12. For every dual-unit control, require browser traces for
    switch -> visible unforced edit -> consumer -> roundtrip from metric and
    imperial initial states. Unit-switch-only traces are incomplete.
13. For unit conversions, audit value, label, minimum, maximum, step, defaults,
    persistence, and round-trip invariance as one physical contract.
14. For dynamic/repeated controls, create a new item while already in metric and
    imperial mode and assert value, min, max, step, validity, canonical state,
    and final consumer behavior.
